# BMS Molecular Translation — swarm final solution

`submission.csv`: 484,838 rows (`image_id,InChI`), order identical to `data/sample_submission.csv`.

## Final pipeline (as submitted)
1. **Primary model (regulus_iota)**: from-scratch image->SMILES seq2seq
   (ResNet34 encoder, 256px letterboxed grayscale; 6-layer Transformer decoder d=512;
   char-level SMILES vocabulary; KV-cache greedy decoding), trained on all 1.94M
   `train_labels.csv` labels converted to canonical isomeric SMILES, with two cosine
   LR-decay polish rounds (phase-3 checkpoint is the primary). SMILES -> InChI via RDKit.
   Holdout (shared 20k split, first-3000): phase-3 model **1.791** (first-1000 1.203);
   previous checkpoint 1.907.
2. **Full test inference**: `solution_code/altair_medoid/infer_iota.py` (sorted by PNG
   size, resumable, raw SMILES streamed; ~25 min on one A100).
3. **Tail ensemble (medoid consensus)**: routed ids = invalid ∪ lowest 8% of primary-model
   confidence (39,607). Candidates per image:
   {primary, primary ckpt_last, primary rot180, **previous iota model**, omega rot180-TTA,
   MolScribe zero-shot (aspect-preserving letterbox)}; pick candidate with minimum sum
   Levenshtein distance to the other candidates; constant-InChI fallback if none valid.
   Non-routed ids keep the primary prediction.
   Honest holdout estimate of the full policy: **~1.33** (halves 1.331/1.321);
   iota-only was 1.791; earlier phase/cascade variants 1.39-1.49.
4. All code (training, tokenizer/precompute SMILES, inference, MolScribe cascade,
   medoid assembly) is in `solution_code/`; see `solution_code/README.md` and
   `solution_code/altair_medoid/SOLUTION_README.md`.

Validation used only the 20k holdout cut from `train_labels.csv`
(`workspaces/regulus_iota/val_20k.csv`); no test labels or external feedback were used.
